{
  "id": "hooper-visual-organization-test",
  "term": "Hooper Visual Organization Test",
  "definition": "The Hooper Visual Organization Test is a task used here to assess visuospatial abilities by helping identify brain areas involved in visuospatial processing. In this study, an nTMS-adapted version was used before surgery to map visuospatial brain networks and support surgical planning aimed at preserving those functions.",
